            <ArticleTitle>Pharmacobezoar in an obese patient with intragastric balloon: a case revealed at endoscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>168-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/cob.12003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pharmacobezoar formation is a very rare complication that occurs in cases of altered gastrointestinal motility or to a background of disturbed anatomy of the gastrointestinal tract. The case of an obese and depressed patient treated by an intragastric balloon for weight loss, who was revealed to have a pharmacobezoar during endoscopy for early balloon removal, is presented. The possible causes of pharmacobezoar formation in such a patient treated with an intragastric balloon are discussed.</AbstractText>
